@page "/rules"
@{
    ViewData["Title"] = "Rules of Conduct";
    ViewData["Description"] = "The rules of conduct for playing Legends of Hollowmere: be decent to other players, play fair, and keep your account safe.";
}
<section class="band">
    <div class="wrap">
        <p class="eyebrow">Living together</p>
        <h1>Rules of conduct</h1>
        <p class="draft">DRAFT. These rules are a first draft written for the owner to edit. They are not yet final or official.</p>
        <div class="prose">
            <p>Hollowmere is shared by everyone who plays in it. These are the few things that keep it pleasant.</p>
            <ol class="steps">
                <li><b>Be decent to other players.</b> No harassment, threats, hate speech, or targeting of anyone for who they are. Disagree with the character, not the person behind it.</li>
                <li><b>Keep it fit for company.</b> Keep what you say in public channels suitable for a mixed audience, and do not share anything sexual or graphically cruel.</li>
                <li><b>Play fair.</b> Do not cheat, exploit bugs for gain, or use programs that play for you. If you find something broken, report it rather than profiting from it.</li>
                <li><b>One character, one person, one account.</b> Do not share your account. Do not impersonate other players or the people who run the game.</li>
                <li><b>Protect your account.</b> Use a password that you use nowhere else. Nobody who runs the game will ever ask for it.</li>
                <li><b>Do not spoil for others.</b> Discovery is half the fun. Share hints if asked, but let people find things for themselves.</li>
                <li><b>Respect privacy.</b> Do not share other people's personal information, in or out of the game.</li>
                <li><b>Listen to the staff.</b> The people who run the game may warn, mute, suspend or remove accounts that break these rules.</li>
            </ol>
        </div>
    </div>
</section>
